// CrossEngin effectors: outbound HTTP action (P4, ADR-0054).
//
// The "search" / API-call tool backend (ACT_NET_FETCH, NOTIFY tier). A real
// call is the gated transport already in the tree (learn_pipeline.lp_fetch:
// DNS + whitelist + rate-limit + TLS); to keep this effector light and tests
// hermetic/offline, the live path is a documented SEAM and the default is a
// SIMULATED mode that returns a caller-supplied canned response. The planner
// runs it simulated; production swaps in lp_fetch behind the same result shape.
//
// ADRs: ADR-0054, ADR-0028 (gated fetch). CrossEngin deps: tool.nova.

import "tool.nova"

// simulated == 1: return the canned body (offline, deterministic).
// simulated == 0: the live fetch seam (lp_fetch) is intentionally not imported
//   here; the caller wires it. Returns an unsuccessful result if asked to go
//   live without that wiring.
fn http_action_run(url, simulated, canned) {
    if len(url) == 0 { return tr_new(0, 0, "no-url") }
    if simulated == 1 { return tr_new(1, len(canned), canned) }
    return tr_new(0, 0, "live-http-not-wired")
}
